{
 "title": "The logistic equation",
 "domain": {
  "x": [
   0,
   100
  ],
  "y": [
   0,
   120
  ]
 },
 "elements": [
  {
   "id": "title",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "The logistic equation",
   "x": 500,
   "y": 712,
   "font_size": 34
  },
  {
   "id": "ax",
   "type": "axes",
   "x_label": "Time",
   "y_label": "Population N"
  },
  {
   "id": "kline",
   "type": "curve",
   "expr": "100",
   "style": {
    "color": "#8f887c",
    "dash": true
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "k_label",
   "type": "label",
   "text": "K — carrying capacity",
   "attach_to": "kline",
   "side": "below",
   "style": {
    "color": "#8f887c"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "eq",
   "type": "math",
   "tex": "\\frac{dN}{dt} = rN\\left(1 - \\frac{N}{K}\\right)",
   "size": 28,
   "x": 300,
   "y": 660
  },
  {
   "id": "exp_curve",
   "type": "curve",
   "expr": "5*exp(0.09*x)",
   "x_from": 0,
   "x_to": 33,
   "style": {
    "color": "#b5482e",
    "dash": true
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "exp_label",
   "type": "label",
   "text": "pure exponential",
   "attach_to": "exp_curve",
   "side": "left",
   "style": {
    "color": "#b5482e"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "curve",
   "type": "curve",
   "expr": "100/(1+19*exp(-0.09*x))",
   "style": {
    "color": "#2f6b8f"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "curve_label",
   "type": "label",
   "text": "N(t)",
   "attach_to": "curve",
   "side": "below-right",
   "style": {
    "color": "#2f6b8f"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "p_infl",
   "type": "point",
   "at": {
    "x": 32.7,
    "y": 50
   },
   "guides": true,
   "style": {
    "color": "#2f6b8f"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "infl_label",
   "type": "label",
   "text": "fastest growth at N = K/2",
   "attach_to": "p_infl",
   "side": "right"
  },
  {
   "id": "verhulst",
   "type": "portrait",
   "of": "Pierre François Verhulst",
   "cameo": true
  },
  {
   "id": "eq_mark",
   "type": "annotation",
   "target": "eq",
   "kind": "box"
  }
 ],
 "commands": [
  {
   "draw": [
    "title"
   ],
   "speak": "Bacteria in a flask double and double — and then, without warning, stop. Forecast from the early doublings and you will be badly wrong."
  },
  {
   "draw": [
    "ax"
   ]
  },
  {
   "draw": [
    "kline",
    "k_label"
   ],
   "speak": "Start with a ceiling: K, the carrying capacity — the largest population this environment can feed."
  },
  {
   "pause": 0.3
  },
  {
   "draw": [
    "eq"
   ],
   "speak": "The whole idea: growth equals r times N, times one minus N over K."
  },
  {
   "draw": [
    "exp_curve",
    "exp_label"
   ],
   "speak": "When N is tiny, that bracket is almost one, so growth is just r times N — the runaway exponential."
  },
  {
   "pause": 0.4
  },
  {
   "draw": [
    "curve",
    "curve_label"
   ],
   "speak": "The real population starts on that same path, then peels away from it."
  },
  {
   "draw": [
    "p_infl",
    "infl_label"
   ],
   "speak": "Halfway to the ceiling the two factors balance, and the population gains members faster than at any other moment of its life."
  },
  {
   "pause": 0.3
  },
  {
   "highlight": {
    "target": [
     "curve"
    ],
    "effect": "glow"
   },
   "speak": "Past that, the bracket shrinks toward zero — plenty of parents, no room left — and the curve lies down on K."
  },
  {
   "draw": [
    "verhulst"
   ],
   "speak": "Pierre-François Verhulst wrote this in 1838, answering Malthus, and it was he who named the S-shape logistic."
  },
  {
   "erase": [
    "verhulst"
   ],
   "speak": "His curve now fits yeast in a flask, epidemics, and a new phone's sales."
  },
  {
   "draw": [
    "eq_mark"
   ],
   "speak": "So the S is not two laws stitched together: it is one product, r N pushing up while one minus N over K pushes back — and the fastest growth is the sign that the slowdown has already begun."
  }
 ]
}